  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Operators, vendors and businesses pay for networks that work and recover fast. They judge you by uptime, troubleshooting method and documentation.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is a calm troubleshooting method with written notes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and telecom and 5G: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools monitor networks and suggest fixes. Routine monitoring shrinks first.
  </p>
  <p>
    Field judgment, safety discipline and accountability for outages hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI for analysis; later, own the decisions.
  </p>

